#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:4
msgid "Installing from the snapshot repository"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:6
msgid ""
"The main ROS apt repository only holds the most recent version of each "
"package, so a sync can move your system onto newer packages than the ones "
"you last tested against. This article describes how to install ROS from a "
"snapshot of the ROS apt repository, which lets you control exactly when your "
"system moves to a newer sync."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:11
msgid ""
"Snapshots are only available for :ref:`Long Term Support (LTS) releases "
"<list_of_distributions>` on Ubuntu."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:15
msgid "Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:18
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:20
msgid ""
"Packages are synced from the ``ros-testing`` :doc:`apt repository </"
"Developer-Tools/Debugging/Testing/Testing>` into the main ROS apt repository "
"periodically for each active distribution. When a sync happens, the older "
"versions of the updated packages are removed from the main repository and "
"can no longer be installed. Also, while maintainers and ROS Bosses strive to "
"avoid regressions, packages failing to build are removed when syncing. This "
"is disruptive if your build or deployment depends on a specific set of "
"package versions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:25
msgid ""
"To improve overall reproducibility and to provide more control over package "
"updates, the snapshot repository at `snapshots.ros.org <http://snapshots.ros."
"org/>`__ keeps a copy of the main ROS apt repository as it was just after a "
"sync. Installing from a snapshot gives you a fixed set of package versions "
"that does not change until you choose a different snapshot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:28
msgid ""
"Most users should install from the main repository by following the :doc:"
"`installation instructions <Ubuntu-Install-Debs>`. The snapshot repository "
"is useful if you bundle ROS packages into an artifact such as a container "
"image, or if you want to move to a new sync deliberately rather than "
"whenever you next run ``apt upgrade``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:31
msgid ""
"Snapshots are taken for a ROS distribution's Ubuntu target platform and "
"architectures. See :ref:`the list of platforms binaries are built for "
"<binary-package-platforms>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:36
msgid ""
"Snapshots do not receive bug fixes or security updates. Keep following ROS "
"releases and upgrade periodically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:40
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:43
msgid "1 Add the snapshot repository key"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:45
msgid ""
"The snapshot repository is signed with its own key, which is *not* the key "
"that the ``ros2-apt-source`` package installs for the main repository. "
"Download it into a keyring of its own:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:48
msgid ""
"$ sudo mkdir -p /etc/apt/keyrings\n"
"$ curl -fsSL \"https://keyserver.ubuntu.com/pks/lookup?"
"op=get&search=0x4B63CF8FDE49746E98FA01DDAD19BAB3CBF125EA\" | sudo gpg --"
"dearmor -o /etc/apt/keyrings/ros-snapshots-archive-keyring.gpg"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:53
msgid "Check that you downloaded the expected key before using it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:55
msgid ""
"$ gpg --show-keys --with-fingerprint /etc/apt/keyrings/ros-snapshots-archive-"
"keyring.gpg"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:59
msgid ""
"Confirm that the fingerprint it prints is ``4B63 CF8F DE49 746E 98FA  01DD "
"AD19 BAB3 CBF1 25EA``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:62
msgid "2 Choose a snapshot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:64
msgid ""
"Browse `snapshots.ros.org <http://snapshots.ros.org/>`__, and choose the "
"distribution and then snapshot you want to install."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:66
msgid ""
"Snapshots are named after the date of the sync they were taken from, such as "
"``2026-08-07``. When a distribution reaches end of life, a last snapshot "
"named ``final`` is taken, which you can use like any other snapshot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:69
msgid ""
"Record your choice in the shell you will use for the remaining steps, for "
"example, ``humble`` and ``2026-08-07``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:71
msgid ""
"$ export ROS_DISTRO=humble\n"
"$ export SNAPSHOT=2026-08-07"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:77
msgid "3 Add the snapshot repository to apt"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:79
msgid "Write an apt source file pointing at the snapshot you chose:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:81
msgid ""
"sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/ros2-snapshots.sources > /dev/null <<EOF\n"
"Types: deb\n"
"URIs: http://snapshots.ros.org/${ROS_DISTRO}/${SNAPSHOT}/ubuntu\n"
"Suites: $(. /etc/os-release && echo ${UBUNTU_CODENAME:-"
"${VERSION_CODENAME}})\n"
"Components: main\n"
"Signed-By: /etc/apt/keyrings/ros-snapshots-archive-keyring.gpg\n"
"EOF"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:91
msgid ""
"If you have already installed ROS, remove the ``ros2-apt-source`` package:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:93
msgid "$ sudo apt remove ros2-apt-source"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:97
msgid ""
"In case you are switching to an older snapshot, give the snapshot repository "
"a pin priority above 1000 so that apt prefers it, otherwise apt will not "
"downgrade to the snapshot's older versions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:99
msgid ""
"sudo tee /etc/apt/preferences.d/ros2-snapshots > /dev/null <<EOF\n"
"Package: *\n"
"Pin: origin snapshots.ros.org\n"
"Pin-Priority: 1001\n"
"EOF"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:107
msgid "Then update the apt caches:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:109
msgid "$ sudo apt update"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:114
msgid "4 Use a matching rosdistro index"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:116
msgid ""
"The rosdistro index is versioned separately from the apt repositories, so "
"``rosdep`` may resolve keys against a newer state of `rosdistro <https://"
"github.com/ros/rosdistro>`__ than the snapshot you installed. Syncs are "
"tagged in ``rosdistro`` using the same ``<distribution>/<date>`` naming as "
"snapshots, so you can :doc:`pin the index </Migration-and-Upgrades/Using-"
"Custom-Rosdistro>` to the tag matching your snapshot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:119
msgid ""
"$ sed -i \"s|ros\\/rosdistro\\/master|ros\\/rosdistro\\/${ROS_DISTRO}\\/"
"${SNAPSHOT}|\" /etc/ros/rosdep/sources.list.d/20-default.list\n"
"$ mkdir -p ~/.config/rosdistro\n"
"$ echo \"index_url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ros/rosdistro/"
"${ROS_DISTRO}/${SNAPSHOT}/index-v4.yaml\" > ~/.config/rosdistro/config.yaml\n"
"$ rosdep update"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:128
msgid ""
"We use ``~/.config/rosdistro/config.yaml`` as a more permanent ``rosdistro`` "
"index pin here. However, the ``ROSDISTRO_INDEX_URL`` environment variable "
"takes precedence over this configuration file. If it is set, unset it, "
"otherwise the index is not pinned to your snapshot. To check which index is "
"used:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:133
msgid ""
"$ python3 -c \"from rosdistro import get_index_url; print(get_index_url())\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:138
msgid "5 Install ROS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:140
msgid ""
"Install packages as you normally would. The versions you get are the ones "
"that were in the main repository at the time of the snapshot:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:143
msgid "$ sudo apt install ros-rolling-desktop"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:147
msgid ""
"If you already had ROS installed from the main repository, move the existing "
"installation onto the snapshot:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:149
msgid "$ sudo apt dist-upgrade"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:153
msgid ""
"Note that this may downgrade packages, since the snapshot can be older than "
"the main repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:156
msgid "Return to the main repository"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:158
msgid ""
"To go back to the main repository, remove the snapshot source and the pin:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:160
msgid ""
"$ sudo rm /etc/apt/sources.list.d/ros2-snapshots.sources\n"
"$ sudo rm -f /etc/apt/preferences.d/ros2-snapshots"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/_Apt-Repositories.rst:5
msgid "You will need to add the ROS 2 apt repository to your system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/_Apt-Repositories.rst:7
msgid ""
"First ensure that the `Ubuntu Universe repository <https://help.ubuntu.com/"
"community/Repositories/Ubuntu>`_ is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/_Apt-Repositories.rst:9
msgid ""
"$ sudo apt install software-properties-common\n"
"$ sudo add-apt-repository universe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/_Apt-Repositories.rst:14
msgid ""
"The `ros-apt-source <https://github.com/ros-infrastructure/ros-apt-source/"
">`_ packages provide keys and apt source configuration for the various ROS "
"repositories."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/_Apt-Repositories.rst:16
msgid ""
"Installing the ros2-apt-source package will configure ROS 2 repositories for "
"your system. Updates to repository configuration will occur automatically "
"when new versions of this package are released to the ROS repositories."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/_Apt-Repositories.rst:19
msgid ""
"$ sudo apt update && sudo apt install curl -y\n"
"$ export ROS_APT_SOURCE_VERSION=$(curl -s https://api.github.com/repos/ros-"
"infrastructure/ros-apt-source/releases/latest | grep -F \"tag_name\" | awk -"
"F'\"' '{print $4}')\n"
"$ curl -L -o /tmp/ros2-apt-source.deb \"https://github.com/ros-"
"infrastructure/ros-apt-source/releases/download/${ROS_APT_SOURCE_VERSION}/"
"ros2-apt-source_${ROS_APT_SOURCE_VERSION}.$(. /etc/os-release && echo "
"${UBUNTU_CODENAME:-${VERSION_CODENAME}})_all.deb\"\n"
"$ sudo dpkg -i /tmp/ros2-apt-source.deb"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:167
msgid "Then update the apt index and upgrade:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:169
msgid ""
"$ sudo apt update\n"
"$ sudo apt dist-upgrade"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:174
msgid "Reset the rosdistro index:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:176
msgid ""
"$ rm ~/.config/rosdistro/config.yaml\n"
"$ rm /etc/ros/rosdep/sources.list.d/20-default.list\n"
"$ sudo rosdep init\n"
"$ rosdep update"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:183
msgid "To move to a different snapshot instead, start from step 2 again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:186
msgid "FAQs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:188
msgid "How often are snapshots published?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:189
msgid ""
"A snapshot is usually taken after a sync, but the interval between snapshots "
"varies. Browse `snapshots.ros.org <http://snapshots.ros.org/>`__ to see what "
"is available for a distribution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:192
msgid "How long are snapshots kept?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:193
msgid ""
"Snapshots for released distributions are available for at least six months "
"from their sync or end of life date."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:195
msgid "Is there a snapshot repository for Rolling?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:196
msgid "No. Snapshots are only published for released distributions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:199
msgid "How is this different from the ``ros-testing`` repository?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:200
msgid ""
"The two point in opposite directions. The ``ros-testing`` repository holds "
"packages that have *not yet* been synced into the main repository, so you "
"can test them before a release. A snapshot holds packages exactly as they "
"were at a *past* sync, so you can keep installing the versions you already "
"tested. See :doc:`Testing with pre-release binaries </Developer-Tools/"
"Debugging/Testing/Testing>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:205
msgid "Can I use a snapshot on a production robot?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:206
msgid ""
"Snapshots receive no bug fixes and no security updates. If you use one, "
"treat moving to a newer snapshot or distro as part of your regular "
"maintenance. Note that ABI compatibility between snapshots is not tested or "
"guaranteed, so when switching a system to a new snapshot, updating all ROS "
"packages is recommended."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:210
msgid ""
"How can I get a snapshot of Debian packages from Ubuntu, e.g., ROS "
"dependencies?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Snapshot-Repository.rst:211
msgid "`Ubuntu has its own snapshot service <https://snapshot.ubuntu.com/>`__."
msgstr ""
